{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Is anything too wondrous for HaShem</b> — if the matter is wondrous and remote, that it should come from HaShem thus, as in the language of 'for all is from You, and from Your hand we have given to You' (I Chronicles 29:14), and similar to it 'from Asher, his bread is rich' (Genesis 49:20) — from Asher comes rich bread. And Onkelos translated 'הֲיִתְכַּסֵּי' (will it be hidden), rendering it like the language of 'for a matter is too wondrous for you for judgment' (Deuteronomy 17:8), and if so, there is in it a hidden mystical secret. And Rashi's language: 'הֲיִפָּלֵא' — 'הֲיִתְכַּסֵּי' (will it be hidden), and is any matter too wondrous and hidden from Me, from being done according to My will. He combined in it two meanings:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes Onkelos and Rashi using the same Aramaic/Hebrew synonym הֲיִתְכַּסֵּי ('will it be hidden/concealed'); both are rendered identically to preserve Ramban's point that they share this rendering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:17.192668130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}